---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro'
import { site } from '../data/site'
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms and Conditions"
  updated="2 November 2026"
  description="Terms for using the New Window Web Design website."
>
  <p>
    These terms apply to your use of this website, operated by {site.name}. By using the website, you agree to them. If
    you commission a website from us, the terms for that work are set out separately in your quote.
  </p>

  <h2>Information on this website</h2>
  <p>
    We aim to keep the information on this website accurate and up to date. Prices shown are starting prices for our
    standard packages. The final price and what’s included are confirmed in a written quote before any work begins.
  </p>

  <h2>Concept projects</h2>
  <p>
    Projects labelled as concepts are designs we have created to demonstrate our work. The businesses, names and details
    shown in them are fictional and are not our clients.
  </p>

  <h2>Using this website</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You may view and share pages of this website for your own, non-commercial use.</li>
    <li>You must not misuse the website, for example by attempting to gain unauthorised access, introducing malicious code or sending spam through our contact form.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    The design, text, graphics and code of this website belong to {site.name} unless stated otherwise. You may not copy or
    reuse them without our permission.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
  <p>We are not responsible for the content of other websites that we link to.</p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>
    We provide this website as it is and cannot guarantee that it will always be available or free from errors. Nothing
    in these terms limits any liability that cannot be limited under the law.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>We may update these terms from time to time. The date at the top of this page shows when they were last changed.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms? {
      site.email ? (
        <>
          Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
        </>
      ) : (
        <>
          Get in touch through our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
        </>
      )
    }
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
